work_units.notes:
Extract DataFrame benchmark query resolution into a single internal helper
module. The helper should own:
  - benchmark ID normalization;
  - TPC-H stream permutation ordering;
  - TPC-DS standard stream generation;
  - TPC-DS variant lookup and fallback behavior;
  - ClickBench DataFrame query registry retrieval;
  - benchmark-instance `get_dataframe_queries()` fallback;
  - MagicMock/synthetic hook rejection if still needed.

Candidate destination: `benchbox/core/dataframe/query_resolution.py` or a
similarly focused core DataFrame module. Keep it internal unless the
public-contract map is updated.

The production mixin and dry-run query extraction must call the helper.
The deprecated runner may call the helper while remaining as a thin
compatibility wrapper.

Add one predicate that can answer "does this adapter/config/platform mean
DataFrame execution?" without relying on two unrelated sources of truth.

The predicate must account for:
  - explicit execution mode in database config;
  - `-df` suffix and deployment suffix handling;
  - PlatformRegistry default mode;
  - actual adapter DataFrame capability;
  - existing family values `expression` and `pandas`;
  - future DataFrame family values without modifying runner.py.

Candidate shape: adapter property/protocol `is_dataframe` plus a factory
resolver for config/platform strings. If a property is added to adapters,
include compatibility fallback for older adapters during the migration.
